> a(x: u8 in 0..7) = x*x
> b(x: u8 in 0..7) = x*x + (x & 8)
> equiv a ~ b
a and b are equal on the domain of a (exhaustive)
> domain a
domain of a:
  x: u8, 0..7
  defined at 8 of 8 points
  no conditions: total on its parameter types
  over all 8 points of the domain
> range a
range of a -> u8:
  0..49   (8 distinct values)
  values: 0..1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36, 49
  fits in u6
  over all 8 points of the domain
> c(x: u8 in 0..15) = x
> d(x: u8 in 0..15) = x + (x & 16)
> equiv c ~ d
c and d are equal on the domain of c (exhaustive)
> domain d
domain of d:
  x: u8, 0..15
  defined at 16 of 16 points
  no conditions: total on its parameter types
  over all 16 points of the domain
> e(x: u8) = x*x where x <= 7
> f(x: u8) = x*x + (x & 8) where x <= 7
> equiv e ~ f
e and f are equal on the domain of e (exhaustive)
  domain: x in 0..7 by the where clause (8 points enumerated)
> domain e
domain of e:
  x: u8, 0..255
  where x <= 7
  defined at 8 of 8 points
  no conditions: total on its parameter types
  over all 8 points of the domain
> g(x: u8) = x where x <= 3 || x >= 252
> h(x: u8) = x where x <= 3 || x >= 252
> equiv g ~ h
g and h are equal on the domain of g (exhaustive)
> range g
range of g -> u8:
  0..255   (8 distinct values)
  values: 0..3, 252..255
  fits in u8
  over all 8 points of the domain
> i(x: u16 in 0..255) = x + 1
> j(x: u16 in 0..255) = (x + 1) & 255
> equiv i ~ j
i and j differ at 1 point, e.g. x=255: 256 vs 0
> equiv j ~ i
j and i differ at 1 point, e.g. x=255: 0 vs 256
> k(x: u8 in 8..15) = x - 8
> l(x: u8 in 8..15) = x xor 8
> equiv k ~ l
k and l are equal on the domain of k (exhaustive)
> range k
range of k -> u8:
  0..7   (8 distinct values)
  values: 0..7
  fits in u3
  over all 8 points of the domain
> m(x: u8 in 0..15) = x*x
> n(x: u8 in 0..15) = x*x + 256
  note: literal 256 does not fit u8; it becomes 0
> equiv m ~ n
m and n are equal on the domain of m (exhaustive)
> equiv n ~ m
n and m are equal on the domain of n (exhaustive)
